WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.753
False computer-checked

00:00:01.565 --> 00:00:02.295
proofs

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:03.722
A collection of

00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:04.747
cases in which

00:00:04.559 --> 00:00:05.986
computer-checked proofs

00:00:05.798 --> 00:00:06.516
turned out to

00:00:06.328 --> 00:00:07.141
be false

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:08.238
and the lessons

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:08.875
they hold for

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:10.349
trusting machine-verified

00:00:10.161 --> 00:00:11.127
mathematics

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:12.334
There are some

00:00:12.146 --> 00:00:13.442
computer programs that

00:00:13.254 --> 00:00:14.114
claim to check

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:14.999
every step in

00:00:14.811 --> 00:00:15.553
a proof

00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:16.942
In many cases

00:00:17.154 --> 00:00:18.145
these bugs have

00:00:17.956 --> 00:00:19.017
been demonstrated to

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:19.902
be exploitable

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:21.770
From this perspective

00:00:21.971 --> 00:00:23.527
HOL Light's proof-checking

00:00:23.339 --> 00:00:24.671
kernel is attractive

00:00:24.577 --> 00:00:25.284
because of its

00:00:25.096 --> 00:00:26.676
stability and simplicity

00:00:26.853 --> 00:00:28.456
only 400 lines

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:28.952
of code

00:00:29.478 --> 00:00:30.492
Full story on

00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:31.199
the dashboard
